course: dictionary
lesson: 10013
title: Temporarily: for now, not for ever
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Read this sentence: «The bridge is temporarily closed.» The clue is the word temporarily, which tells you the closing will not last. A sign like this does not mean the bridge is shut for ever. It means it is shut for a short time and will open again later.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The bridge is closed for now, until it opens again.» That still makes sense, so temporarily means for now. When a meaning fits every clue, you can trust it.
explain: In «As if in a dream … all sense of right and wrong … seemed temporarily suspended», the word temporarily shows that the feeling was paused for a while, not gone for ever. Look for the clue word first, then decide what the whole sentence is saying.
fact: Temporarily means for a short time only, not for ever.
fact: Temporarily also means for now, until something changes.
fact: The opposite of temporarily is permanently, which means for ever.
fact: A sign that says «temporarily closed» means it will open again later.
fact: In science, a change can be temporary: melting ice can freeze again.
exercise: «The road is temporarily shut for repairs.» What does temporarily mean here? | For ever, with no end | Quickly, in a hurry | *Only for now, until the repairs are done | Loudly, for everyone to hear
exercise: A sign says «temporarily out of order». What does it tell you? | *The machine will work again later | The machine is broken for ever | The machine is full of water | The machine is very old
exercise: Which word means the opposite of temporarily? | Happily | Quickly | Briefly | *Permanently
test: «The shop is temporarily closed for the holidays.» What does this tell you? | The shop is full of children | The shop has closed for ever | *The shop will open again after the holidays | The shop sells only holiday cards
test: A man at the till says he is temporarily embarrassed, as a joke. What does he mean? | He is lost in the shop | *He has run out of money for now | He has forgotten his name | He is very shy with strangers
exam: Jayden says a lift is temporarily out of order. What does he mean? | *The lift is broken for now and may be fixed later | The lift is broken for ever | The lift is very tall | The lift is a kind of sweet
